/-!
# Tensor injectivity for monomial ideals in log regular charts

Source: ILO, Travaux de Gabber, Exposé VIII, proof of Lemma 3.4.3, printed p. 110,
using Kato (1994), 6.1(ii); Exposé VIII, 3.5, printed p. 115
(blueprint: lem-trf-log-regular-monomial-tor).

The additive monoid algebra Z[P] is written `MonoidAlgebra ℤ (Multiplicative P)`.
For an ideal H of P, its monomial ideal is the span of the monomials indexed by H;
because H + P is contained in H, its underlying group is precisely the direct sum Z[H].
`LinearMap.liftBaseChange` applied to the restricted algebra map is the canonical
multiplication map, sending a tensor z^h to a * alpha(h).
-/

@[expose] public section

set_option autoImplicit false

universe u

open CategoryTheory Opposite

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

/-- Tensoring a monomial ideal with a log regular affine chart is injective, with
image exactly the ideal generated by the chart images of its monomials.
Source: ILO VIII, proof of Lemma 3.4.3, printed p. 110; VIII 3.5, printed p. 115
(blueprint: lem-trf-log-regular-monomial-tor).

Proof:
1. At a geometric point, localize the monoid at the face mapping to units. Use
`lem-trf-fs-face-sharpening` and `lem-trf-log-regular-sharp-chart` to obtain a sharp
chart of the characteristic monoid. The localization, splitting and unit twist of
`lem-trf-log-chart-face-tor-comparison` identify Tor_1 of the monomial quotient over
the original monoid ring with Tor_1 over the sharp chart ring. The latter vanishes
by `lem-trf-kato-tor-independence-chart`.
2. The scheme local ring is Noetherian. Its map to the strict henselization is flat
and local by `lem-sc-strict-henselization-dvr`, hence faithfully flat by
`lem-pc-local-flat-faithful-flat-reflects-surjective`. Apply
`lem-trf-tor-flat-base-change` and `lem-sc-faithfully-flat-tensor-zero` to descend
Tor_1 vanishing to that local ring. Then `lem-trf-tor-localization-on-spec` descends
vanishing from all prime localizations to A.
3. Apply `lem-weil-pbc-tor-long-exact-first-variable` to 0 -> I -> Z[P] -> Z[P]/I -> 0.
The projectivity of Z[P] and the vanishing just obtained make I tensor A -> A
injective. Tensor symmetry identifies it with the displayed A tensor I -> A.
4. Pure tensors a tensor z^h generate the source and map to a * alpha(h). Their
images therefore generate exactly the ideal spanned by alpha(H). For H empty the
source and this ideal are both zero.
-/
theorem logRegular_monomialIdeal_tensor_injective
    (X : FineSaturatedLogScheme.{u}) (A : Type u) [CommRing A]
    (eA : X.scheme ≅ Spec (.of A)) (hlog : X.IsLogRegular)
    (P : Type u) [AddCommMonoid P] (hP : IsFineSaturatedMonoid (Multiplicative P))
    (α : Multiplicative P →* A)
    (c : Multiplicative P →* X.logStructure.monoidSheaf.obj.obj
      (op (Scheme.Etale.mk (𝟙 X.scheme))))
    (hc : X.logStructure.IsChart (Scheme.Etale.mk (𝟙 X.scheme)) c)
    (hα : ∀ p : P,
      X.logStructure.alpha.app (op (Scheme.Etale.mk (𝟙 X.scheme)))
        (c (Multiplicative.ofAdd p)) =
      eA.hom.appTop ((Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of A)).inv (α (Multiplicative.ofAdd p))))
    [Algebra (MonoidAlgebra ℤ (Multiplicative P)) A]
    (hAlg : algebraMap (MonoidAlgebra ℤ (Multiplicative P)) A =
      (MonoidAlgebra.lift ℤ A (Multiplicative P) α).toRingHom)
    (H : Set P) (hH : ∀ h ∈ H, ∀ p : P, h + p ∈ H) :
    Function.Injective
      (LinearMap.liftBaseChange A
        ((Algebra.linearMap (MonoidAlgebra ℤ (Multiplicative P)) A).comp
          (Ideal.span {z : MonoidAlgebra ℤ (Multiplicative P) |
            ∃ h ∈ H, z = MonoidAlgebra.single (Multiplicative.ofAdd h) 1}).subtype)) ∧
    LinearMap.range
      (LinearMap.liftBaseChange A
        ((Algebra.linearMap (MonoidAlgebra ℤ (Multiplicative P)) A).comp
          (Ideal.span {z : MonoidAlgebra ℤ (Multiplicative P) |
            ∃ h ∈ H, z = MonoidAlgebra.single (Multiplicative.ofAdd h) 1}).subtype)) =
      (Ideal.span ((fun h : P ↦ α (Multiplicative.ofAdd h)) '' H) : Submodule A A) := by
  sorry

end AlgebraicGeometry
